# PINE_MANIFEST.sha256 — Q-TOM-SPX-1 canonical concept-stage Pine harness
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   `**/*.pine` is gitignored (public-clone posture, edge protection), so the
#   gate-bearing harness `tom_test_spx500.pine` is NOT in git and does not
#   survive across worktrees. On 2026-06-16 the original authoring copy was
#   found unrecoverable (uncommitted on a since-removed worktree, no hash on
#   record). The verbatim source was reconstructed from the operator's paste
#   and this hash committed so "load the canonical Pine harness" (Q-TOM-SPX-1
#   brief §6 / SPX500 ledger OQ1) becomes a VERIFIABLE instruction even though
#   the .pine bytes themselves stay gitignored. The hash is the durable record.
#
#   NOTE: this closes the durability gap only partially — the SOURCE is still
#   not in git. Full closure (committing the source) is a public-clone-posture
#   decision; this script is concept-stage / ABSENT-verdict / no live edge, so
#   committing it would be safe, but that is an operator call, not done here.
#
# CONVENTION
#   SHA256 is over the UTF-8 bytes with LF line endings (CRLF normalized to LF
#   before hashing). The committed copy is LF, so raw == normalized.
#
# VERIFY (CRLF-robust — works regardless of how your editor saved line endings)
#   python -c "import hashlib,pathlib;p=pathlib.Path('lab/analysis/tom_spx/tom_test_spx500.pine');print(hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes().replace(b'\r\n',b'\n')).hexdigest())"
#   # compare the printed digest to the line below
#
#   (If your working copy is LF, plain `sha256sum -c PINE_MANIFEST.sha256`
#    from this directory also works.)
